<title>JAPAN: Japan buys 180,000 tonnes wheat, 20,000 T barley.</title>
<headline>Japan buys 180,000 tonnes wheat, 20,000 T barley.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Japanese Food Agency said on Thursday it bought 180,000 tonnes of wheat, including 60,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat, 60,000 of Canadian wheat and 60,000 of Australian wheat, and 20,000 tonnes of Australian barley at its weekly tender, all for September shipment.</p>
<p>The tender results were as follows, in tonnes.</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p>    Country    Quantity</p>
<p>    U.S.	 60,000	   Western white	    20,000</p>
<p>					Dark northern spring   20,000</p>
<p>					Hard red winter	  20,000</p>
<p>    Canada     60,000	   Western red spring     60,000</p>
<p>    Australia  60,000	   Standard white	   60,000</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p>    Country    Quantity</p>
<p>    Australia  20,000	   Feed			 20,000</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodity Desk, +81-3-3432-7431</p>
</text>
